    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d402">

                <pb facs="0392" n="276" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg276"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 123.G35/67a.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the American Chargé
                        d’Affaires</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Extract.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-10-12">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 12, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Department will give the following to the press to-morrow: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>In consideration of his several hard years of service in Honduras, in the
                            Department of State, and at Habana, it was the intention of the
                            Department to transfer Mr. Hugh S. Gibson, now Secretary of Legation at
                            Habana, to be Secretary of Legation at Brussels. But owing to Mr.
                            Gibson’s special familiarity with American interests in Cuba, the
                            President has directed that he be retained at Habana.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
